From e6580874391cf5289fea9f2889a287ede9cb8c7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: samtheruby <peasea1012@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:09:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(coreelec): auto frame rate switches resolution too

Kodi switches the display to a video's own resolution when its whitelist
has that resolution; TizenTube's auto frame rate only changed the refresh
rate. Now the page script adds the height of the best quality YouTube can
play (getAvailableQualityData) to TizenTube's SetFrameRate, and the display
extension (version 2, SetVideoFormat) switches to an allowed mode of that
height first, 16:9 before 4096 wide. Otherwise it keeps the current
resolution and changes only the rate, as before.

YouTube offers no quality above what the display shows, so the platform now
reports the largest mode auto frame rate may use (current, original or
allowed); a 4K video on a 1080p desktop can then ask for 2160p.

On framebuffer windows the switch points fb0's scaler at the new mode. On
DRM the window keeps its size and an atomic commit scales the primary
plane to the mode (checked on the Xiaomi stick: 1080p window in 2160p24,
page flips keep the scaling); the hotplug check keeps the current mode's
size. After a resolution switch players place their video again, and on
DRM its rectangle is scaled to the mode.
